    <h2>What Is the Mixing Bowl Mashup Blizzard® Treat?</h2>
    <p>The Mixing Bowl Mashup Blizzard combines several popular Blizzard mix-ins into a single cup — think a curated combination of cookie pieces, fudge, and candy elements from existing fan-favorite flavors. The exact recipe may vary slightly by region, but the concept is a "greatest hits" Blizzard that delivers multiple flavors in every bite. It is one of the most talked-about Summer 2026 seasonals due to its variety-in-one-cup approach.</p>
  <p>Browse all Summer 2026 seasonals and year-round Blizzards on <a href="/">The Queen Dairy Menu</a>.</p>

    <h2>What Makes the Mashup Unique</h2>
  <p>Most Blizzards are built around a single candy bar, cookie, or flavor theme. The Mixing Bowl Mashup deliberately crosses those lines — it is closer to the "combo" orders that DQ fans have been requesting at the counter for years (Oreo + Cookie Dough being the most popular unofficial combo). The Mashup formalizes that concept into a seasonal menu item.</p>
  <p>If you enjoy ordering custom Blizzard combinations, the Mixing Bowl Mashup is worth trying. If you prefer a clean, predictable single-flavor Blizzard, the <a href="/items/oreo-blizzard">Oreo</a> or <a href="/items/cookie-dough-blizzard">Cookie Dough</a> delivers more consistency.</p>

    <h2>How It Compares to Other Blizzards</h2>
    <div class="table-wrap"><table class="size-table"><thead><tr><th>Blizzard</th><th>Mini Price</th><th>Small Cal</th><th>Flavor Profile</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Mixing Bowl Mashup</td><td class="price-cell">$4.49</td><td>520</td><td>Multiple mix-ins — most complex seasonal</td></tr><tr><td>Dipped Strawberry Cheesecake</td><td class="price-cell">$4.49</td><td>540</td><td>Single-profile fruit + cheesecake</td></tr><tr><td>S'mores Blizzard</td><td class="price-cell">$4.49</td><td>500</td><td>Three-component campfire flavor</td></tr><tr><td>Oreo® Cookie Blizzard</td><td class="price-cell">$3.49</td><td>420</td><td>Single mix-in, year-round</td></tr></tbody></table></div>

    <h2>Ordering Tips</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>First timer?</strong> Order a Mini (4.49) — it's 4–5 spoonfuls, perfect for a taste test before committing to a full cup.</li>
      <li><strong>Best size for one person:</strong> Small (5.29) at 520 calories hits the sweet spot of satisfaction without going overboard.</li>
      <li><strong>Upgrade option:</strong> Ask to blend in a hot fudge swirl for richer chocolate depth, or add extra mix-ins (~$0.50).</li>
      <li><strong>Check the flip:</strong> DQ guarantees every Blizzard is thick enough to hold upside down — if your crew doesn't flip it, it's free.</li>
    </ul>

